WEBVTT

00:00:04.002 --> 00:00:13.774
This is Typecase, a calm writing app for Linux. Your library is a folder of plain Markdown files, and at first, every group and sheet looks the same.

00:00:14.074 --> 00:00:18.086
To make a group stand out, right-click it and choose Icon and Color.

00:00:18.386 --> 00:00:21.075
Pick one of the nine accent colors from GNOME,

00:00:21.596 --> 00:00:26.376
then one of twenty-eight icons. Apply, and the group shows them right away.

00:00:27.076 --> 00:00:34.907
Give the other groups and sheets their own look, too. Characters, places, ideas and open questions now stand out at a glance.

00:00:35.207 --> 00:00:37.790
The colors follow the light and dark style.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:49.667
And nothing is hidden away: a sheet keeps its icon and color in its front matter, a group in its own folder, so they travel along when you move, copy or sync them.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.799
Typecase. Free software, made for GNOME.

00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:55.682
With love, by kleinod.studio.
